./xmodel/sol-approaches.md:116:- **Campaign:** **Yes, but conjectural.** [TDBOUND.md](../TDBOUND.md), [sol-tdbound-review.md](sol-tdbound-review.md), [sol-pcc-orbits.md](sol-pcc-orbits.md), [sol-wtc1.md](sol-wtc1.md), and [sol-g5-emission.md](sol-g5-emission.md) test pole-mass/PCC formulations. Apparent numerical support was downgraded when most coincidences proved census-forced.
./xmodel/sol-approaches.md:117:- **Precise obstruction.** The earliest missing theorem, WTC-1, must transport a Laurent common-power packet and its denominators to named ordinary or infinitely-near pencil base centers with mobile multiplicities and proximity parents. Coverage and non-double-counting are unproved. Even $\operatorname{td}\le mn$ is not an absolute bound while $m,n$ remain unbounded.
./xmodel/sol-approaches.md:118:- **Cheapest untried extension — 8/10.** Prove or refute WTC-1 on one explicit nontrivial GGV chain by constructing the complete base-point/proximity graph and comparing its squared mass with the Laurent packet.
