./xmodel/sol-wtc1.log:140716:The hostile pass found and repaired three subtle points: GGV uses a maximum face (so the toric boundary ray must be \(-w\)); the Laurent graph has distinct domain and original-plane projections (only the latter carries pencil proximity); and an existential \(c_p\) version of PCC-COVER was circular. The draft now uses a target-side blowup word, gcd-free mobile ideals, and a canonical conservative packet weight \(c_p^{\max}\).
