./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:592:- **Precise obstruction.** The earliest missing theorem, WTC-1, must transport a Laurent common-power packet and its denominators to named ordinary or infinitely-near pencil base centers with mobile multiplicities and proximity parents. Coverage and non-double-counting are unproved. Even $\operatorname{td}\le mn$ is not an absolute bound while $m,n$ remain unbounded.
./xmodel/sol-monodromy.log:593:- **Cheapest untried extension — 8/10.** Prove or refute WTC-1 on one explicit nontrivial GGV chain by constructing the complete base-point/proximity graph and comparing its squared mass with the Laurent packet.
